new file mode 100644
index 0000000..19e9623
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-audit.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in, sign-up, the shared layout and document headers. This is a demo application; these changes do not establish legal compliance or verify the external account service.
+
+| Finding | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| Analytics executed on every page, including account pages. | Removed the third-party analytics loader and the commented ad loader. No consent state or tracking identifier is introduced. |
+| Layout contacted Google Fonts and initialized ad slots automatically. | Removed remote font stylesheets, preconnects and the layout ad island. Brand headings use local serif fonts. |
+| Forms did not explain the external credential transfer. | Added a disclosure beside each form, a privacy link and a warning to use made-up credentials. Only username and password are collected. |
+| Credential requests relied on fetch defaults. | Shared request helper explicitly omits cookies and referrers, bypasses the browser cache and rejects redirects. No response token is persisted. |
+| Backend error details were displayed, and sign-in retained passwords after submission. | Display generic errors without parsing response bodies; clear passwords after every completed attempt. Add password-manager hints and enforce the displayed sign-up password requirements. |
+| Every visit initialized session storage. | Removed eager reading-list initialization. Its existing POST endpoint creates storage when an article is saved. |
+| Documents lacked privacy headers. | Added no-referrer in HTTP headers and document metadata, disabled sensitive browser permissions, prevented caching of HTML and reading-list API responses, and marked account pages noindex. Corrected the UTF-8 declaration. |
+| Privacy policy was generic, and privacy preferences linked nowhere. | Describe the implemented data flows and known limits; link the footer to the policy. |
+
+Remaining boundaries:
+
+- The external account service is outside this repository. Its credential storage, retention, deletion and response behavior were not verified. The forms preserve the existing demo API contract and do not create a persistent login session.
+- Hosting logs and session lifetime depend on deployment configuration. Removing the session cookie does not guarantee deletion of server-side data.
+- Some article content includes remote images and deliberate interactive cookie demonstrations. Those are disclosed in the policy and remain outside this change's layout/form scope.
+- The Content Security Policy constrains object embedding, base URLs and native form destinations; it is not a complete script allowlist. Optional tracking must not be reintroduced without a separate privacy review and an appropriate user choice.
+
+Validation: `pnpm test` checks both credential request destinations and payloads, omission of ambient credentials/referrers, cache and redirect behavior, and failure handling without automatic retries or credential logging. `pnpm run build` verifies production compilation. No browser, development/preview server, server entrypoint import or live credential submission was used.
