+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration news site. This page describes the data flows implemented in this application.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="accounts">Demo accounts</h2>
+    <p>Sign-in and sign-up ask only for a username and password. Choose a made-up username that does not identify you and a password you do not use anywhere else. No name, email address, or marketing preference is requested.</p>
+    <p>Only when you submit a form, those two fields are sent over HTTPS to the external demo account service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api</code>, using its <code>login</code> or <code>register</code> endpoint. The service also receives connection information such as your IP address. The request omits cookies and referrer information and is configured not to use the browser cache or follow redirects.</p>
+    <p>The form clears the password after each submission attempt. This application does not save account credentials or returned tokens in browser storage, and a successful demo sign-in does not establish a persistent signed-in session here. Password managers may save credentials according to your browser settings.</p>
